  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Polar form and argument"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "With $r = |z|$ and $\\theta$ the angle $OP$ makes with the positive real axis, $x = r\\cos\\theta$, $y = r\\sin\\theta$, so $z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)$. $\\theta$ is the argument; the principal argument lies in $(-\\pi, \\pi]$. Find the acute angle $\\alpha$ with $\\tan\\alpha = |y/x|$, then place it in the right quadrant: $\\alpha$, $\\pi - \\alpha$, $-(\\pi - \\alpha)$ or $-\\alpha$.",
    "kn": "ಧ್ರುವೀಯ ರೂಪ z = r(cos θ + i sin θ), r = |z|. ಮುಖ್ಯ ಕೋನಾಂಕ (−π, π] ಅಂತರದಲ್ಲಿರುತ್ತದೆ; ಚತುರ್ಥಕ ನೋಡಿ ಹೊಂದಿಸಿ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Quadrant I: α; II: π − α"
    },
    {
     "en": "Quadrant III: −(π − α); IV: −α"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In polar form, z equals r times cos theta plus i sin theta. Find the acute angle from tan alpha equals y over x, then adjust it for the quadrant to get the principal argument between minus pi and pi.",
    "kn": "ಧ್ರುವೀಯ ರೂಪ z = r(cos θ + i sin θ), r = |z|. ಮುಖ್ಯ ಕೋನಾಂಕ (−π, π] ಅಂತರದಲ್ಲಿರುತ್ತದೆ; ಚತುರ್ಥಕ ನೋಡಿ ಹೊಂದಿಸಿ."
   },
   "formula": "z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta), \\quad r = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}"
  },
